<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import Panel from "$ui/components/Panel.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Layouts</h1>
  <p class="lead">A <code>layout.abide</code> wraps its folder and everything below it — write the shared frame once and every page in the subtree gets it. Layouts nest <strong>outer→inner</strong> (the root layout, then each section layout), and the page renders wherever a layout places its <code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code>. The indigo frame around this content is <code>pages/layouts/layout.abide</code>, itself nested inside the doc-site root layout.</p>
  <Demo id="section-layout-src" title="The section layout — <code>pages/layouts/layout.abide</code>" client="src/ui/pages/pages/layouts/layout.abide" tab="client">
    <p>☝ The indigo frame wrapping this whole page is this layout, live. Its <code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code> is where the page renders.</p>
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>A layout renders the level below it — the next layout, or the page — at its <code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code> (the interpolation form is <code>{'{'}children(){'}'}</code>). A layout has no props; like a page it reads the current route with <code>route()</code>.</p>
  </aside>
  <Panel id="layout-nav" title="Layouts stay alive across navigation">
    <div class="row">
      <a data-testid="to-nested" href="/pages/layouts/nested">→ child page (cross-route)</a>
      <a data-testid="to-carousel" href="/pages/layouts/alpha">→ carousel item (param nav)</a>
    </div>
  </Panel>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>A layout isn't re-rendered when you navigate within its subtree — its instance persists. Increment the counter above, then move around: to the child page (cross-route) or into a carousel item (param nav). The count holds because the framework keeps shared layouts mounted and grafts only the diverging page into the <code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code> — effects don't re-run, scroll position is preserved, and only its <code>route()</code>-driven bits update in place.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
